1218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Interviewer: The client operates as an IT services company based in Mumbai, offering a range of services to clients primarily located in North America and Europe. Their expertise encompasses software development, consulting, and support services. They undertake diverse projects, including custom software development, system integrations, and IT consulting engagements.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Candidate: Now, let's delve into the client's cost structure to identify areas for potential improvement. The client's cost structure likely comprises employee salaries, infrastructure expenses, sales and marketing expenditures, and potentially outsourcing costs for specific projects. A detailed breakdown of each category would provide insights into the percentage allocation and identify areas for cost optimization.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Interviewer: Great. Now, focus on the revenue side of the equation. How does the client generate revenue, and what is their pricing strategy for their services?)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
