/ActualText (Consultant: We have 52 weeks in a year, so that would translate to 52 x 5 = 260 working days. Let us remove 20 days for government holidays, employee holidays, etc. This leaves us with 240 working days. Let us divide the days into long days and short days. Assuming 60% of the days to be long and the remaining 40% to be short days. Would this be a fair assumption?)
