2040 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Interviewer: A and C. Also what do you think are the differentiation factors between us and our competition? Consultant: I think they would be : i\) Product efficiency; ii\)Look and feel; iii\)After purchase problems Interviewer: Correct. Consultant: Is there any difference in the efficiency of our product when compared to our competitors? Interviewer: Yes, a competitor has amped up the power of their mass produced tractor engine at the same price point. There is no change in the look and feel or after purchase service of any competitors. What courses of action should the tractor manufacturer adopt to counter this?  Consultant: In order to increase the number of units sold and to regain our original market position:  i\) We must increase the power of our mass produced tractors to at least match our competitors  ii\) We must invest in R&D to improve the features of our premium tractors. Interviewer: Thank you, that will be all.)
/E (Interviewer: A and C. Also what do you think are the differentiation factors between us and our competition? Consultant: I think they would be : i\) Product efficiency; ii\)Look and feel; iii\)After purchase problems Interviewer: Correct. Consultant: Is there any difference in the efficiency of our product when compared to our competitors? Interviewer: Yes, a competitor has amped up the power of their mass produced tractor engine at the same price point. There is no change in the look and feel or after purchase service of any competitors. What courses of action should the tractor manufacturer adopt to counter this?  Consultant: In order to increase the number of units sold and to regain our original market position:  i\) We must increase the power of our mass produced tractors to at least match our competitors  ii\) We must invest in R&D to improve the features of our premium tractors. Interviewer: Thank you, that will be all.)
