2554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Interviewer: Alright, moving on to the market entry strategy, how should our client enter the VR shopping market?)
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2555 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Consultant: Given the complexity of VR technology and the potential benefits of leveraging existing expertise, I would recommend exploring strategic partnerships or acquisitions. This could provide access to essential technology, experienced personnel, and established relationships with key players in the VR ecosystem. )
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Interviewer: Keep in mind that it's important to consider the potential benefits of maintaining control over the core technology and ensuring alignment with our client's overall vision.)
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2557 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Consultant: Yes, a hybrid approach could allow our client to leverage the expertise of existing VR companies while maintaining control over key aspects of the platform and ensuring it aligns with their long-term goals. Moreover, targeting tech-savvy consumers who have shown interest in early adoption of innovative technologies would be a strategic initial target segment. Tech-savvy consumers are more likely to be receptive to VR shopping experiences and provide valuable feedback for further development.)
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Interviewer: Good strategy. What potential risks and challenges do you foresee in entering the VR shopping market, and how would you propose a risk mitigation plan? )
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2559 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Consultant: Potential risks include technology barriers, consumer hesitancy, and the evolving nature of VR regulations. To mitigate these risks, I would recommend a phased market entry approach, starting with a limited product range and gradually expanding as the technology matures. )
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
